"The problem. USB drives with the exFAT or FAT32 file system have no “sparse” files. A torrent downloads pieces in a random order, and when the next piece lies far from the current end of the file, the system fills the whole gap before it with zeros. While this goes on, Transmission does not respond, and sometimes the whole console hangs." = "The problem. USB drives with the exFAT or FAT32 file system have no “sparse” files. A torrent downloads pieces in a random order, and when the next piece lies far from the current end of the file, the system fills the whole gap before it with zeros. While this goes on, Transmission does not respond, and sometimes the whole console hangs."
"The solution. The fix downloads pieces in order and no more than 64 MB ahead. The file grows gradually, so there are no large zero fills." = "The solution. The fix downloads pieces in order and no more than 64 MB ahead. The file grows gradually, so there are no large zero fills."
"The price. The speed is lower, and if nobody has the nearby pieces right now, the download waits for a while." = "The price. The speed is lower, and if nobody has the nearby pieces right now, the download waits for a while."
"Without the fix Transmission downloads pieces in any order. When a piece lies far from the end of the file, the system fills the whole gap with zeros. This takes about 10 seconds for every 1 GB (assuming 100 MB/s writing; longer on slow drives). For a 50 GB torrent that is about 8 minutes." = "Without the fix Transmission downloads pieces in any order. When a piece lies far from the end of the file, the system fills the whole gap with zeros. This takes about 10 seconds for every 1 GB (assuming 100 MB/s writing; longer on slow drives). For a 50 GB torrent that is about 8 minutes."
"All this time Transmission itself does not respond: its web interface freezes (the “Transmission for PS5” settings page keeps working). If the hang is longer than the manager’s wait time (2 minutes by default), it restarts the daemon, and the fill starts again. This time can be increased in the “Advanced settings”." = "All this time Transmission itself does not respond: its web interface freezes (the “Transmission for PS5” settings page keeps working). If the hang is longer than the manager’s wait time (2 minutes by default), it restarts the daemon, and the fill starts again. This time can be increased in the “Advanced settings”."
"Do not open the torrent folder in file managers (BFpilot and the like) during this time and do not copy files to this drive: they use the same drive and can hang the whole console." = "Do not open the torrent folder in file managers (BFpilot and the like) during this time and do not copy files to this drive: they use the same drive and can hang the whole console."
"If this happens, do not panic: wait for the approximate time from the estimate above. As a last resort the hang stops when the USB drive is physically unplugged." = "If this happens, do not panic: wait for the approximate time from the estimate above. As a last resort the hang stops when the USB drive is physically unplugged."
"The hang lasts until the torrent files take all their space on the drive (for torrents of many files, as it progresses). After that the download goes without problems and faster than with the fix." = "The hang lasts until the torrent files take all their space on the drive (for torrents of many files, as it progresses). After that the download goes without problems and faster than with the fix."
"There are no download folders. Add them on the “Transmission for PS5” page (port 9092), the “Download folders” section." = "There are no download folders. Add them on the “Transmission for PS5” page (port 9092), the “Download folders” section."

